National Catastrophe Insurance Plan.

Here are some of the details:

* Because of rising costs of insuring against specious legal
decisions, such as requiring today's companies to pay for the possible
radiation exposure of children who sat too close to color t.v.s in
1960, many Americans are "exposed."

* They often cannot buy insurance to cover these odd, unpredictable
